  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"0.1.0\"\n\npackage:\n  name: jpeg2000-hdf5-plugin\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/hmaarrfk/hdf5_jpeg2000/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 29515b9e6eb7e68f9286e0368d580f062738f69c2659d4396fdf8c0c09ef1b52\n\nbuild:\n  number: 1\n  script:\n    - if: win\n      then:\n        - cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja %CMAKE_ARGS% -DHDF5_PLUGIN_INSTALL_DIR=lib/hdf5/plugin\n        - cmake --build build\n        - cmake --install build\n      else:\n        - cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja ${CMAKE_ARGS} -DHDF5_PLUGIN_INSTALL_DIR=lib/hdf5/plugin\n        - cmake --build build\n        - cmake --install build\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - cmake\n    - ninja\n  host:\n    - hdf5\n    - libojph\n    # The CMake config of hdf5 2.1.0, the newest hdf5 2 on linux-ppc64le,\n    # looks for zlib's headers.\n    - if: target_platform == \"linux-ppc64le\"\n      then: zlib\n  ignore_run_exports:\n    from_package:\n      - zlib\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      files:\n        - if: linux\n          then: lib/hdf5/plugin/libh5jpeg2000.so\n        - if: osx\n          then: lib/hdf5/plugin/libh5jpeg2000.dylib\n        - if: win\n          then: Library/lib/hdf5/plugin/h5jpeg2000.dll\n  - requirements:\n      run:\n        - h5py\n    script:\n      # Until hdf5 sets HDF5_PLUGIN_PATH on Windows:\n      # https://github.com/conda-forge/hdf5-feedstock/pull/334 (hdf5 2.x)\n      # https://github.com/conda-forge/hdf5-feedstock/pull/335 (hdf5 1.14.x)\n      - if: win\n        then: set \"HDF5_PLUGIN_PATH=%PREFIX%\\Library\\lib\\hdf5\\plugin\"\n      - python -c \"import h5py; assert h5py.h5z.filter_avail(32031)\"\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/hmaarrfk/hdf5_jpeg2000\n  repository: https://github.com/hmaarrfk/hdf5_jpeg2000\n  license: BSD-3-Clause\n  license_file: LICENSE.txt\n  summary: HDF5 filter plugin 32031 that stores each chunk as a JPEG 2000 codestream\n  description: |\n    A dynamically loaded HDF5 filter plugin, registered as filter 32031, that\n    stores each chunk of a dataset as one JPEG 2000 (including HTJ2K)\n    codestream, encoded and decoded with libojph. It installs to\n    lib/hdf5/plugin, the directory HDF5 searches by default on Linux and\n    macOS, and to Library/lib/hdf5/plugin on Windows, which the hdf5\n    package adds to HDF5_PLUGIN_PATH on activation.\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - hmaarrfk\n",
